# Pagination

- Paginate every list whose result can grow without a small hard bound. Query only the current page on the server; never fetch the full collection and slice it in the browser.
- Use stable deterministic ordering before applying `offset` and `limit`. Return or retain the matching total so controls and range text remain correct.
- Default operator/admin tables to 50 rows unless the owning workflow has a justified density requirement. Bound user-supplied page sizes at the service boundary with an explicit maximum.
- Backend-driven page routes use an optional `/offset/<int:offset>` segment and preserve non-default `limit` in the query string. Filters, tabs, and searches preserve the page size but reset the offset when their result set changes.
- Build controls with `framework.addons.system.api.utils.misc.pagination.pagination_actions` and `pagination_summary`; do not invent page-local pager payloads.
- Put pagination in the table/list section header: `1-50 of 213` as the subtitle and icon-only `fa-chevron-left` / `fa-chevron-right` actions labeled `Previous page` / `Next page`.
- Hide the section header when pagination is unnecessary and it has no independent title or actions. Never render disabled, decorative, or duplicate pager controls.
- Keep pagination links as application paths so soft navigation refetches the backend page payload. Do not add a GUI-only pager to `TableSection` for server-owned data.
- Test a single-page result and the first and last pages of a multi-page result, including row counts, range text, preserved parameters, and previous/next destinations.
